  "verbalization": "Yesanchinoside J is shown to have a target relationship with T-24 through multiple pathways, with varying levels of confidence. The first pathway links Yesanchinoside J to the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is targeted by a compound with a high score (0.6123). This compound is further shown to target T-24, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving this subunit. The second pathway connects Yesanchinoside J to PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, which is targeted by another compound with a slightly lower score (0.5949), and this target is also linked to T-24. The third pathway similarly links Yesanchinoside J to CDC2L2, which is targeted by Phlegmanol C, which in turn targets T-24. These findings suggest that Yesanchinoside J may act through multiple molecular targets, potentially influencing T-24 through distinct pathways. The evidence supports a relationship between Yesanchinoside J and T-24, but the exact mechanism and the strength of the interactions remain to be fully elucidated.",
